        "created_at": "2013-03-15T13:35:42.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"arenson9\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/arenson9/48/1900_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> arenson9:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div><b>VanceAttack wrote:</b><br><blockquote>My wife had our team kill me.\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote></div>\nCool story!Incapacitated doesn't have to mean killed. AZ just needed to stop being active. Maybe Bunker's blast just knocked him far enough away.ALSO, I like that it was Bunker, the Freedom Five's strategist, who delivered the necessary, incapacitating blow.\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>It's much more dramatic when you mean it as \"Killed\" though. Plus, my wife did say \"Kill him.\" Maybe I should consider some marriage counseling since that came so easy to her…</p>",
